# Tauri 2 desktop (Infinity Express)

App map: [docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md). WeiDU / backups: [docs/weidu-install.md](docs/weidu-install.md).

## Stack

- Shell is **Tauri 2** (not Electron). Frontend: Vite + React under `src/`.
- Rust entry: [`src-tauri/src/lib.rs`](src-tauri/src/lib.rs) via `app_lib::run()`.
- Scripts: `npm run tauri:dev` / `tauri:build`. Browser-only: `npm run dev`.
- Detect desktop: `isTauri()` from `@tauri-apps/api/core` via `isDesktopApp()` in [`fsDialogs.ts`](src/lib/desktop/fsDialogs.ts).

## Plugins vs app commands

| Need | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Native open/save/pick-dir dialogs | `tauri-plugin-dialog` (`@tauri-apps/plugin-dialog`) |
| Open http(s) links in the system browser | `tauri-plugin-opener` (`opener:default` — intercepts `target="_blank"`). If the click is under `stopPropagation` (table rows, dialog panels), call `openUrl` via [`openExternalUrl.ts`](src/lib/desktop/openExternalUrl.ts) instead |
| Write a file the user just picked in **this session** | `tauri-plugin-fs` `writeTextFile` — dialog path is **auto-scoped for the session only** |
| Read/list/delete under a **persisted** user path (e.g. `D:\games\…` after restart) | App `#[tauri::command]` + **`std::fs`** — do **not** fight static `plugin-fs` scopes |
| Persist prefs (paths, catalog) | **localStorage** — do not add `tauri-plugin-store` unless storage must live outside the webview |

Official note: for Rust-side file work, prefer `std::fs` / `tokio::fs` over stretching plugin-fs to arbitrary drives.

## Capabilities (current)

[`src-tauri/capabilities/default.json`](src-tauri/capabilities/default.json):

- `core:default`, `dialog:default`, `fs:allow-write-text-file`, `opener:default`
- App commands: `allow-list-subdir-names`, `allow-remove-mod-dir` → [`permissions/mod-fs.toml`](src-tauri/permissions/mod-fs.toml)
- Acquire: `allow-probe-mod-remote`, `allow-acquire-mod`, `allow-cancel-mod-acquire`

By default, commands registered with `invoke_handler` are callable; still declare explicit `permissions/*.toml` + capability entries when adding commands (clear ACL, matches this repo).

## Frontend helpers (`src/lib/desktop/`)

| Helper | Behavior |
| --- | --- |
| `isDesktopApp()` | `isTauri()` |
| `saveTextFile(name, contents)` | `save()` then `writeTextFile`; `false` if cancelled |
| `pickDirectory(title?)` | `open({ directory: true })`; `null` if cancelled / not Tauri |
| `listSubdirNames(path)` | invoke `list_subdir_names`; `[]` if not desktop / empty |
| `removeModDir(downloadDir, folderName)` | invoke `remove_mod_dir` (CI folder match); no-op if not desktop |

Guards: every helper no-ops or returns empty when `!isDesktopApp()`. UI (e.g. Browse) should disable + tooltip outside desktop.

## Cookbook: add a custom FS command

1. Implement in [`src-tauri/src/mod_fs.rs`](src-tauri/src/mod_fs.rs) (or a new module):

```rust
#[tauri::command]
pub fn my_command(path: String) -> Result<Vec<String>, String> {
  // std::fs… map_err(|e| e.to_string())
}
```

2. Register in `lib.rs`:

```rust
.invoke_handler(tauri::generate_handler![
  mod_fs::list_subdir_names,
  mod_fs::remove_mod_dir,
  // mod_fs::my_command,
])
```

3. ACL — `src-tauri/permissions/something.toml`:

```toml
[[permission]]
identifier = "allow-my-command"
description = "…"
commands.allow = ["my_command"]
```

4. Reference `"allow-my-command"` in `capabilities/default.json` `permissions` array (app perms have **no** `plugin:` prefix).

5. Thin TS wrapper with `invoke` from `@tauri-apps/api/core`. **Args are camelCase** in JS matching snake_case Rust params:

```ts
await invoke('remove_mod_dir', { downloadDir, folderName })
// Rust: remove_mod_dir(download_dir: String, folder_name: String)
```

6. Command name for invoke is the function name (`remove_mod_dir`), not `mod_fs::…`.

## Path-safety patterns (this repo)

- Reject empty names, `.` / `..`, `/` `\`, multi-segment names before joining.
- Resolve delete target as **child of** download dir; refuse if canonical path escapes parent or equals parent.
- Windows: match folder names **case-insensitively**, then delete using the **on-disk** spelling (`find_subdir_ci`).
- Missing download dir / missing folder: list → `[]`; remove of missing folder → `Ok(())`.

## Mods disk semantics

- Settings `modsDownloadDir` (`infinity-express.app-dirs`) is the scan root.
- Download ID (`codename`) = subdirectory name under that root.
- Presence logic (pure TS): [`diskPresence.ts`](src/lib/mods/diskPresence.ts); hook refreshes on load + `ie-paths-changed`.
- Remove from disk deletes the folder; catalog row stays.

## Prefer not to re-research

- Dialog scope ≠ persisted FS access across restarts.
- Broad `$HOME/**` plugin-fs scopes are a poor fit for multi-drive Windows game/mod paths — use app commands.
- Errors from commands: return `Result<T, String>`; frontend `invoke` rejects with that string (often not an `Error` instance — coerce with `String(err)`).
- PowerShell: use `;` not `&&` when chaining (`cd src-tauri; cargo test`).

